+### Refunds 
+
+You have 90 days from the original payment to submit a refund using the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md).
+
+#### Refund process 
+
+When you refund a Scalapay payment, Scalapay updates the customer’s installment plan. For a full refund, Scalapay cancels the remaining installments and refunds the amounts already paid. For a partial refund, Scalapay adjusts the installment plan based on the reduced order total.
+
+#### Track refunds 
+
+To check a refund’s status in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments), open the payment and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.
+
+Stripe sends a `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event when the refund reaches its final status. For a successful refund, the [Refund](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) object has a `status` of `succeeded`. If the refund fails, its status changes to `failed`, and Stripe returns the amount to your Stripe balance. You must refund the customer using another method.
+
+### Disputes 
+
+Customers can dispute a Scalapay payment within 210 calendar days of the purchase date. Each payment can be disputed only once.
+
+#### Dispute process 
+
+1. **Dispute opened**: Scalapay opens the dispute, and Stripe immediately withholds the disputed amount from your balance. You have 7 calendar days to submit evidence.
+2. **Decision**: Scalapay reviews your evidence and issues a final decision within 30 calendar days after the dispute is created.
+
+#### Dispute notifications 
+
+When a Scalapay dispute is opened, Stripe notifies you through:
 
 - Email
-- The Stripe Dashboard
-- An API `charge.dispute.created` event (if your integration is set up to receive [webhooks](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md))
-
-Stripe holds back the disputed amount from your balance until Scalapay resolves the dispute.
-
-We request that you upload compelling evidence proving that you fulfilled the purchase order [using the Stripe Dashboard](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/responding.md#respond). This evidence can include the:
-
-- Tracking ID
-- Shipping date
-- Record of purchase for intangible goods, such as IP address or email receipt
-- Record of purchase for services or physical goods, such as phone number or proof of receipt
-- Record of refund (for purchase you’ve already refunded)
-
-To handle disputes programmatically, [respond to disputes using the API](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/api.md).
-
-This information helps Scalapay determine if a dispute is valid. Make sure the evidence you provide contains as much detail as possible from what the customer provided at checkout. You must submit the requested information within 12 calendar days. If Scalapay resolves the dispute with you winning, we return the disputed amount to your Stripe balance. If Scalapay rules in favor of the customer, the disputed amount stays with the customer.
