-- eur: CA+- The [Stripe Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/disputes)
+- A [charge.dispute.created](https://docs.stripe.com/api/events/types.md#event_types-charge.dispute.created) webhook event
+
+The dispute reason appears in the Dashboard and in the `reason` field of the [Dispute](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/object.md) object. The evidence submission deadline appears in the Dashboard and in the object’s `evidence_details.due_by` field.
+
+#### Respond to disputes 
+
+You have 7 calendar days after the dispute is created to submit evidence.
+
+Provide evidence that demonstrates you fulfilled the order. This can include tracking information, shipping and delivery dates, order records, customer communications, and proof of any refund you’ve issued.
+
+Submit evidence and manage Scalapay disputes in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/disputes) or with the [Disputes API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md). In the Dashboard, on the **Needs Response** tab, select the disputed payment, and then click **Counter dispute** to submit evidence or **Accept dispute** to accept the loss.
+
+To submit evidence through the API, upload supporting files using the [Files API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/files/create.md). Include the returned file IDs in the evidence when you update the [Dispute Evidence](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md) object.
+
+#### Dispute outcomes 
+
+If Scalapay resolves the dispute in your favor, Stripe returns the disputed amount to your Stripe balance.
+
+If they rule in favor of the customer, the balance charge becomes permanent.
+
+You can submit evidence only once for a Scalapay dispute. Gather all supporting evidence before submitting it because you can’t add more afterward.
