+## Connect 
+
+You can use [Stripe Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/how-connect-works.md) with Scalapay to process payments on behalf of connected accounts. Connected accounts must have the `scalapay_payments` capability enabled. For more information, see [Connect payment method capabilities](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/account-capabilities.md).
+
+## Customer experience 
+
+#### 1. Select payment method
+
+The customer selects Scalapay at checkout.
+
+#### 2. Redirect to Scalapay
+
+The customer is redirected from your website or app to Scalapay's hosted payment page.
+
+#### 3. Choose a payment plan
+
+The customer chooses Pay in 3 or Pay in 4 and authorizes the payment on Scalapay's hosted page.
+
+#### 4. Payment complete
+
+The customer sees a confirmation from Scalapay and returns to your website or app. Stripe immediately notifies you whether the payment succeeded or failed.
+
+### Transaction identifiers 
+
+After a Scalapay payment succeeds, expand `latest_charge` on the `PaymentIntent` and retrieve the Scalapay transaction ID from `latest_charge.payment_method_details.scalapay.transaction_id`. Give this ID to customers so they can identify the payment when contacting Scalapay support.
+
+## Enable Scalapay 
+
+If you use Stripe front-end products, enable Scalapay in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically displays the payment methods most relevant to each customer.
+
+If your integration lists payment methods manually, learn how to [configure Scalapay as a payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/scalapay/accept-a-payment.md).